From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-11
Subject: [PATCH jm-v9 020] panvk: v9 warn once when indirect prerast/tess draws exceed the chunk caps biblioklept

Purpose: Make the 014/017 indirect chunk limits visible.
Indirect gpu_prerast draws (GS, XFB, polygon mode, viewport select, VS
stores) are unrolled into V9_PRERAST_INDIRECT_CHUNKS chunks and indirect
tessellated draws into V9_TESS_INDIRECT_CHUNKS chunks. Work past those is
dropped. Log a once-per-process mesa_logw_once at record time for every
indirect draw on such a path. The caps are not raised: each chunk unrolls
a full job set into the command buffer.
Source/Reference: none (panvk-local)
Tested GPU: build-checked (universal Android build v6-v14); G615 (v11) PanProbe regression with the universal .so; device run on Mali-G57 MC2 (gpu_id 0x90930010) pending, see worklogs/v9-jm/PROGRESS.md
Tested Kbase UAPI: JM 11.38
Mesa base range: 5a07217f + g615-v11-csf series + jm-v9 001-019
Dependencies: jm-v9 014, 017
Validation test: logcat check (pending G57)

---
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index e9b9baf..c5605c5 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -3587,6 +3587,13 @@ v9_prerast_chunked(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
    if (!v9_prerast_reserve_jobs(cmdbuf, 2))
       return;
 
+   /* The cut happens on the GPU, the CPU cannot tell when: say it once. */
+   mesa_logw_once("panvk: v9 indirect gpu_prerast draws (GS, transform "
+                  "feedback, polygon mode, viewport select, VS stores) are "
+                  "drawn in at most %u chunks of %u vertices; the rest of a "
+                  "larger draw is dropped",
+                  V9_PRERAST_INDIRECT_CHUNKS, max_verts);
+
    struct panvk_precomp_ctx ctx = panvk_per_arch(precomp_cs)(cmdbuf);
    panlib_chunk_setup(&ctx, panlib_1d(1), PANLIB_BARRIER_JM_BARRIER, cd.gpu,
                       draw->indirect.buffer_dev_addr,
@@ -3826,6 +3833,11 @@ v9_tess_draw(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
                   : (uint64_t)draw->instance.count *
                        DIV_ROUND_UP((uint64_t)ppi, max_patches);
    }
+   if (indirect)
+      mesa_logw_once("panvk: v9 indirect tessellated draws are drawn in at "
+                     "most %u chunks of %u patches; patches past them are "
+                     "dropped",
+                     V9_TESS_INDIRECT_CHUNKS, max_patches);
    uint64_t iters = chunks * iters_per_chunk;
    if (iters > V9_TESS_MAX_ITERATIONS) {
       mesa_loge_once("panvk: v9 tessellated draw needs %" PRIu64
